<item>
            <title>[KYLIN-5526]  After setting the upper limit of concurrent asynchronous queries, submitting multiple asynchronous queries at the same time may cause the number of asynchronous queries to be greater than the set upper limit</title>
                <link>https://issues.apache.org/jira/browse/KYLIN-5526</link>
                <project id="12316121" key="KYLIN">Kylin</project>
                    <description>&lt;p&gt;When encountering a large number of concurrent asynchronous query requests, the number of asynchronous query jobs will exceed the parameter limit, which needs to be fixed&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&#160;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&#22312;&#36935;&#21040;&#24182;&#21457;&#24322;&#27493;&#26597;&#35810;&#35831;&#27714;&#22823;&#30340;&#26102;&#20505;&#65292;&#24322;&#27493;&#26597;&#35810;job&#30340;&#25968;&#30446;&#20250;&#22823;&#20110;&#21442;&#25968;&#38480;&#21046;&#65292;&#38656;&#35201;&#20462;&#22797;&lt;/p&gt;</description>
                <environment></environment>
        <key id="13533942">KYLIN-5526</key>
            <summary> After setting the upper limit of concurrent asynchronous queries, submitting multiple asynchronous queries at the same time may cause the number of asynchronous queries to be greater than the set upper limit</summary>
